abstract: >-
  Let Λ be a lattice in R^5 and b a vector outside Λ such that distinct
  points of Λ ∪ (Λ + b) are at distance at least 2. We prove that the
  covolume of Λ is at least 16√2. Hence no packing of unit balls centred at
  two translates of a lattice in R^5 is denser than the D5 lattice packing.
  Equality holds for exactly five such configurations up to congruence:
  three splittings of √2 D5 and two non-lattice packings.
